> magically closed after the "cusku" and do nothing, right?

You could use "kem" or "kep" to make jargon words or cadigans. Say you have a 
file format which has blocks and chunks; you could call them "kembli" 
and "grike'e" or the like. Or you can use words like "kemdza" 
and "borbo'ekepcomdai" for "whatchamacallit" and "doohickey".

